      "side": 1,
      "message": "First , thanks for comments.\n\n\u003eSo Skia does not support rendering to an unpremul surface,\n\nThat surprise me. Since this CL indeed works I did a bit dig into. It seems in our case this CL make SkColorSpaceXformSteps.flags.premul \u003d false and SkColorSpaceXformSteps.flags.unpremul \u003d false . My understanding is that this doesn\u0027t apply any alpha related op(Not 100% sure but the writePixel code path should be here https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main:third_party/skia/src/gpu/ganesh/SurfaceContext.cpp;l\u003d374;drc\u003d2450f2f5d0ce0da9b8cf493c533f9528ff17bab6 )?\n\n\u003eIs this flow correct:\n\nThe code path could be described like:\nAny alpha type of source image ---\u003e rendering/writePixels to SkSurface(We don\u0027t want any alpha ops during drawing, which means copy the exactly content of source image to the intermediate SkSurace) ---\u003e Upload SkSurface to WebGPU (WebGPU will extract source image alpha type and do alpha op if necessary.). So I think what we want is to issue an rendering/writePixels to SkSurface with no alpha ops been applied.\n\n\n\u003eMaybe it would be best if we could set up a meeting to understand your specific use case and see how we can support that workflow in Skia\n\nDoes slack work? It might be more efficient?",
